00:00:08.419 --> 00:00:10.580 align:start position:0%
we recently got a chance to test out the  battlefield 1 closed alpha and I spent  most of my time playing as a scout for  veterans of the Battlefield franchise  this class shouldn't be a far cry from  what you've come to expect but there are  some key differences  as most good scouts you want to be well  scouting this means surveying an area  marking enemies and backing up your team  from a distance if things get hairy the  only map in the Alpha is Saint Quentin  scar and lucky for you this French  countryside is a haven for snipers a  basic rule of thumb is to stick to the  edges of the map this makes you less of  a target for enemies but it also gives  you the best field of view that is you  won't need to constantly be rotating to  cover the entire battlefield glancing up  hills and around buildings at the center  of town  but of course rules are made to be  broken obviously there's no one good  spot that will give you a good Vantage  of every objective but there are  certainly plenty of good places to snipe  from I would avoid towers and win meals  because that tends to be the first place  most people look and whether someone is  in one of these are not people like to  watch them collapse so instead let's  stick to more unassuming buildings for  now  one in particular that I found to be  effective is located near C from here  you can cover three objectives and there  seems to be no shortage of targets  wandering around in the open if you  don't think you can hit a target from  here make sure to mark them for your  teammates another area that worked  pretty well for me was the hill right  above e it doesn't take too long for  this hillside to get cratered up from  artillery and heavy weapons so camp out  in a crater and you should have some  decent cover and a nice view of the town  a lot of people like to hide behind this  door so keep an eye on that it's also  worth mentioning that for some reason  shooting through doors and windows  hasn't been all that effective as a  scout now it's time to pick a weapon in  the Alpha we had access to three sniper  rifles each with two variations to be  frank there really isn't a huge  difference between these rifles the  Russian 1895 is a lever-action rifle and  the Gewehr and smle are bolt-action  rifles  all three of these rifles have similar  fire rights and can deal quite a bit of  damage  the biggest difference however between  these weapons are the effective range in  battlefield 1 snipers have a sweet spot  if you hit someone at a certain range it  will do extra damage it's also worth  noting that just like previous games  you'll have to take bullet travel time  and bullet drop into account although  judging from the snipers I used bullet  drop was pretty minimal  I rarely had to compensate for it  lastly let's take a look at the  equipment unfortunately Scouts only have  access to two gadgets in the Alpha but  let's start with the flare gun  you only have one flare so make sure to  use it sparingly when you fire it  enemies should light up in that  direction on your mini-map during my  time I did not find the flare gun all  that useful but it does deal fire damage  which is kind of cool the other gadget  are anti armor rounds you can load into  your rifle called K rounds the range for  these aren't too far but if you're at  the right distance it can deal a little  bit of damage I found it best to use  these on vehicles that were already  disabled or some of the smaller quicker  vehicles  as with any class you'll develop your  own methods the more you play as Scout  but these are just a few of the  fundamental differences and tips that  should get you started once you get  behind that scope if you enjoyed this  video and you're itching for more  battlefield one content make sure to  LIKE and subscribe down below  you
 

